<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate 21.91 pct in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate 21.91 pct in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate fell in this week's primary auction and demand rose, Banco de Mexico said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	21.91	    -102	    21.84     22.00</p>
<p>90-Day	23.50	    - 66	    23.28     23.65</p>
<p>182-Day     24.16	    - 47	    23.66     24.46</p>
<p>335-Day     25.68				25.49     25.81</p>
<p>Last week the 342-day paper was assigned at 25.86 pct.  </p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	900 million pesos   2.97 bln pesos     3.30</p>
<p>90-Day	900 million pesos   4.06 bln pesos     4.51</p>
<p>182-Day     900 million pesos   4.75 bln pesos     5.28</p>
<p>335-Day     600 million pesos   2.61 bln pesos     4.35</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 4.36 on demand of 14.38 billion pesos compared to 3.85 the week before, on demand of 12.72 billion pesos the week before. Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			    9 basis points</p>
<p>    90-Day			   15 basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			  30 basis points</p>
<p>    335-Day			  13 basis points</p>
<p>((-- Robert Kozak, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
